# Protect binary assets from end-of-line conversion.
#
# Without this, git treats these as text with unspecified EOL handling, which is
# what let GitHub's web editor offer to "normalize" a PDF to CRLF on 2026-09-05.
# Rewriting 0x0A -> 0x0D 0x0A inside a PDF does not fix anything; it corrupts the
# file and desynchronises the byte offsets in its cross-reference table.

*.pdf   binary
*.docx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.zip   binary

# Text files: normalise in the repo, check out native. Keeps the "mixed line
# endings" warnings from reappearing on the files that legitimately are text.
*.md    text
*.html  text
*.css   text
*.js    text
*.json  text
*.yml   text
*.yaml  text
